Subject: Cantor Succeeding SOP Activation Transaction P0 Data Design

@ [data_design_uuid] e40d73b0-13dd-4d7a-84d2-31d8a76a0933
@ [canonical_uuid] 28da111f-c6b2-4df7-b708-a2d47f8e0bbb

& [Forms]
  + ActivationPolicy holds profile use_status policy_ref activation_authority_ref recovery_owner_ref registry_ref allowed upstream profile required acquisition atomicity durability governance evidence nonauthority and policy digest
  + SourceReacquisitionPlan holds profile plan_ref repository_root_ref exact preservation snapshot path subject source digest bytes proposal digest immutable and raw-byte requirements evidence and digest
  + CurrentSopRegistrySnapshot holds profile snapshot_ref registry_ref registry_path generation current revision digest source path evidence and snapshot digest
  + AtomicRegistryTransitionPlan holds profile transaction_ref expected snapshot digest generations registry final and temporary paths candidate and authority identities exact write protocol atomicity durability and digest
  + SopSupersessionPlan holds exact predecessor and successor revision digest source generation reason preservation flag evidence and digest
  + SopRollbackPlan holds recovery owner exact rollback target failed candidate generation triggers evidence preservation flag and digest
  + ActivationTransactionRequest embeds the complete upstream receipt and every above form plus exact remaining physical obligations and nonauthority
  + ActivationTransactionReceipt projects exact identities status authority policy status ten verified checks seven physical denials all transitive digests and its own digest

& [ClosedValues]
  + acquisition mode is exact_raw_bytes_reopen_no_follow
  + atomicity is same_volume_replace_required
  + durability is file_and_parent_flush_required
  + write protocol is write_new_file verify_new_file flush_new_file atomically_replace_registry flush_parent_directory reopen_and_verify_registry
  + rollback triggers are boot_validation_failure operator_abort persistence_failure post_write_verification_failure registry_precondition_mismatch source_reacquisition_mismatch
  + status is transaction_correspondence_verified_awaiting_physical_execution
  + authority is supplied_activation_plan_correspondence_only

& [DigestDomains]
  + cantor.succeeding-sop-activation.policy.v1
  + cantor.succeeding-sop-activation.source-plan.v1
  + cantor.succeeding-sop-activation.registry-snapshot.v1
  + cantor.succeeding-sop-activation.transition-plan.v1
  + cantor.succeeding-sop-activation.supersession-plan.v1
  + cantor.succeeding-sop-activation.rollback-plan.v1
  + cantor.succeeding-sop-activation.request.v1
  + cantor.succeeding-sop-activation.receipt.v1

& [Bounds]
  + request or receipt machine form maximum is 16777216 UTF-8 bytes
  + policy source supersession and rollback evidence maximum is thirty-two identities each and minimum is one
  + path maximum is 1024 UTF-8 bytes and supersession reason maximum is 512 UTF-8 bytes
  + generation maximum is u64 minus one so successor generation addition cannot overflow
  + exact closed sets carry six write operations six rollback triggers six remaining activation obligations and ten verification checks

& [AuthorityProjection]
  + upstream cryptographic review correspondence is replayed rather than widened
  + transaction form correspondence proves only internal supplied-data consistency
  + physical contact source reacquisition registry observation persistence current selection boot verification rollback execution and physical eligibility remain false
